{"finding_id":"F2","verdict":"refuted","refutation_attempt":"The reported vulnerability claims OS command injection via base64_decode_block, yet the decoded data is never used as an input to any OS command‑execution API (e.g., system(), CreateProcess(), exec(), etc.). The code only converts the decoded bytes into a wide string and places them into the Windows clipboard (lines 57‑63). There is no execution path that interprets the decoded payload as a command, so the sink cannot lead to command injection.

Additionally, no neutralization check is required for the sink itself, because the operation performed is merely decoding and clipboard manipulation, not command execution. The lack of command execution renders the CWE‑787 claim irrelevant in this context.

Hence, the finding is a false positive.","evidence_lines":[57,58,59,60,61,62,63],"confidence":1.0}
